# superglue-py Python conventions

## Thin wrapper rule

If logic belongs in orchestration (retries, tool loops, streaming state machine), implement in **Rust core**, expose via PyO3.

## Tools

- Register tools with schemas the Rust registry understands.
- Callbacks into Python run on the binding layer — keep them short; heavy work belongs in tools, not hooks.

## Testing

- Run examples as smoke tests after native rebuild.
- Prefer Wiremock or offline harness patterns from Rust `tests/` when adding Python integration tests.

## Packaging

- `pyproject.toml` + maturin — do not hand-edit generated artifact paths.
- Version bumps should stay aligned with Rust crate semver policy.
